    <fr:title text="Gotcha: Form-encoded body, not JSON">Gotcha: Form-encoded body, not JSON</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Variable tokens inside <html:code>WFJSONValues</html:code> do not resolve on current iOS — both <html:code>WFTextTokenString</html:code> and <html:code>WFTextTokenAttachment</html:code> serialize to the empty string when the Download URL action builds a JSON body.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:code>WFHTTPBodyType: "Form"</html:code> with <html:code>WFFormValues</html:code> resolves tokens correctly. The capture server accepts <html:code>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</html:code>, so the fix is generator-only.</html:p>
    <html:p>The Download URL builder (note <html:code>"Form"</html:code> body type, not <html:code>"JSON"</html:code>):</html:p>
    <html:pre><![CDATA[def download_url_json(url, json_entries, uuid_=None):
    return action(
        "is.workflow.actions.downloadurl",
        {
            "WFURL": tok_plain(url),
            "WFHTTPMethod": "POST",
            "WFHTTPBodyType": "Form",
            "WFFormValues": _dict_field_value(
                [(k, v, "text") for k, v in json_entries]
            ),
            "Advanced": True,
            "UUID": uuid_ or uid(),
        },
    )]]></html:pre>
  </fr:mainmatter>
